# Sliding along a wall: from the same place as walk_wall, the player runs at
# the wall at an angle (about 29 degrees to it, away from the corner of the
# room), has to be stopped in x by it and carry on along it in y, at the part
# of the running speed that is along the wall.
scenario slide_wall
map bloodgulch
# <name> <x> <y> <z> <yaw, radians>: a little above the ground, so that the
# player settles on it in the first ticks
start base_wall 98.49 -157.64 1.76 -0.5
ticks 100
# settle, then run (the wall is at x = 100.486, facing back along -x)
input 30 100 forward=1.0

# what the Rust simulation may differ from the C engine by (starting values,
# to be tuned by the features' tickets as the comparison shows what is
# reachable); a run of the C engine against itself allows none
tolerance position 0.25
tolerance velocity 0.25
tolerance facing 0.02
tolerance state 0
